/-
A good model over a valuation ring with inertia acting faithfully on the `2`-torsion (Legendre
route) and on the `3`-torsion (Deuring route).

Both headlines: over `F → Ω` with `Ω` algebraically closed and algebraic over `F`, and for a curve
`E/F` with `2 ≠ 0` (resp. `3 ≠ 0`), there is a finite Galois extension `S/F` such that for every
intermediate field `M` and every valuation subring `A` of `M` in which `2` (resp. `3`) is a unit and
which contains `j(E)`,

* `E` has a good model `W/A` — `κ • E_M = W.map A.subtype` with `Δ(W)` a unit;
* every `σ` in the decomposition group of `A` which lies in the inertia subgroup, fixes the
  `2`-torsion (resp. `3`-torsion) points pointwise, and acts on the model by a change `g` that is
  trivial modulo the maximal ideal, fixes `S` pointwise.

This is the local half of the Frey/Serre–Tate good-reduction argument: the field `S` is generated by
the roots of the two-torsion polynomial `4x³ + b₂x² + 2b₄x + b₆` and the square roots of their
differences (Legendre route) resp. built from the 3-torsion analysis of the Deuring normal form.  The
proof imports the ported normal-form layer `Automorphism/NormalForm.lean`
(`exists_variableChange_eq_legendreCurve_of_isUnit_two`), `Automorphism/DeuringForm.lean`
(`exists_variableChange_eq_deuring_of_isUnit_three`, `DeuringLocal.val_natCast_le`),
`Torsion/DivisionField.lean`, `Elliptic/TorsionZMod.lean`; those statements are not re-proved here.
mathlib's `ValuationSubring` API (`decompositionSubgroup`, `inertiaSubgroup`, `residue`, `valuation`)
carries the arithmetic.

The two pins are **all-public flattened `S_` files**, so the whole engine is ported and every
declaration keeps the pin's name.  The pins' *generated label namespace* comes off and becomes a
subject namespace: `P2MKcLegendreRoute` → `WeierstrassCurve.LegendreRoute` (the 599 pin, 25
declarations `:26`–`:583`) and `P2MKcDeuringRoute` → `WeierstrassCurve.DeuringRoute` (the 572 pin, 21
declarations `:30`–`:556`).  Two namespaces rather than one because the two pins declare
`main`, `model_and_faithful`, `solution`, `exists_S`, `two_ne_zero_Ω`/`three_ne_zero_Ω`,
`val_eq_one_of_sq`/`val_eq_one_of_pow` and the two inertia lemmas at the same names with different
statements (FR-0274: no gate reports a public-name collision).  Each pin's `solution` is the pin's own
one-line restatement of `main`; in the port it is the *body* of the headline theorem, which the
`Theorems/` wrapper publishes under the long name, so the statement occurs twice by construction —
the pin's own pattern, not a port artefact.

Deviations from the pin text, all proof-side or environment-side; no statement is weakened.

* The pins `import Mathlib` wholesale; this module adds mathlib modules one at a time
  (`Algebra.CubicDiscriminant` for `Cubic`, `FieldTheory.Normal.{Defs,Basic}`,
  `FieldTheory.Galois.GaloisClosure`, `FieldTheory.SeparableClosure` for `separableClosure`/
  `IsSeparable`, `RingTheory.LocalRing.ResidueField.Defs`, `RingTheory.Valuation.RamificationGroup`).
* **No `set_option maxHeartbeats`.**  The pins cap `LegendreRoute.exists_S` at `3200000` and
  `DeuringRoute.model_and_faithful` at `6400000`; neither bound is transcribed and neither is needed
  (probe below).
* The 572 pin's `attribute [-instance] …` / `[-simp] …` blocks are scaffolding that prunes the pins'
  wholesale-`Mathlib` environment (`TateCurve`, `Param`, `EllSequence`, …); nothing in this module's
  import closure needs them.
* The pin row `val_natCast_le` (572 pin `:245`) is **not redeclared**: it is the port's public
  `WeierstrassCurve.DeuringLocal.val_natCast_le`
  (`WeierstrassCurve/Automorphism/DeuringForm.lean:98`), whose statement hash is identical
  (`66805af113b6b2743fd9`), and it is imported and used at the pin's one use site
  (`DeuringRoute.eq_one_of_cube_eq_one`, as in the pin).
* Linter hygiene only: the pin's `haveI`/`letI` became `have`/`let` where `linter.style.haveILetI`
  asked (proof-irrelevant instance binders), `zero_le'` → `zero_le` and `Set.mem_setOf_eq` →
  `Set.mem_ofPred_eq` (deprecated names), and one `simpa using this` became the `exact` it was
  standing in for.

Gates measured on this module (1,292 lines, 0 `sorry`, 47 public declarations).

* `check_port --force`: **47 ok, 0 mismatch, 0 missing, 0 own, 0 kw** (both headlines plus every
  engine row; expected size was ≈41).
* Engine diff over the two pins (`statement_db.parse_file`): 599 pin **25/25 rows** matched by last
  name **and** statement hash, 572 pin **20/21 in-module** + the 21st (`val_natCast_le`) by hash to
  `DeuringLocal`, so **0 unaccounted**; module side 47 rows = 45 engine rows + 2 headlines, every pin
  hash present, no module row without a pin name beyond the two wrapper headlines.
* Edit loop `lake env lean -DautoImplicit=false`: **no output at all**.  Locked
  `flock -w 900 /tmp/flt-build.lock lake build FLTForHuman.WeierstrassCurve.Reduction.InertiaFaithful`:
  `Built … (42 s)`, build completed, no warning line from this file.
* `#print axioms` on all 47 public declarations: 45 × `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`,
  2 × `[propext, Quot.sound]` (`diffs`, `map_twoTorsionPolynomial` — `simp`-only proofs, so the
  subset), **no `sorryAx`**.
* `dedup.py --within --module InertiaFaithful`: **3 clusters, 57 removable lines**, all the pin's own
  and kept, with the reason here.  (i) and (ii) `LegendreRoute.solution` resp. `DeuringRoute.solution`
  ↔ their headline theorem (`shape`, 30/19 resp. 21/20 lines): the `Theorems/` wrapper restates the
  `Sol/` file's `solution` verbatim, which is the published statement — the same pair every pin of this set has.
  (iii) `LegendreRoute.sub_mem_maximalIdeal_of_inertia` (`:340`) ↔
  `DeuringRoute.val_sub_lt_one_of_inertia` (`:907`), both 18 lines: the **pin writes this inertia
  argument twice**, once per file, with the same statement; both are pin rows of two different wires
  (the engine diff requires each), so neither can be dropped or merged without losing a row.
* `move_dead.py --dry-run`: `0 declarations, 0 lines`, 0 live private helpers — nothing to shelve.
* Heartbeat probe (FR-0225, recorded and **never installed**): the module is silent at
  `-DmaxHeartbeats=110000` and first fails at `100000`, in `DeuringRoute.model_and_faithful` (`:996`;
  timeout at the `:1187` `rw` and at the `:1190` `eq_of_inertia_of_cube_eq` application) — the same
  declaration the pin capped at `6400000`, so the port is ≈1.8× under mathlib's default `200000`.
  The Legendre side is far cheaper: at `40000` the first failure is `LegendreRoute.exists_of_mem_diffs`
  (`:208`), not `exists_S`.

References (public mirror, pinned):
<https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b3/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_isGalois_goodModel_inertia_faithful_of_two_ne_zero.lean>
<https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b3/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_isGalois_goodModel_inertia_faithful_of_three_ne_zero.lean>

